# Charness v8.15.0

## What changed

- `charness task run` now stamps each JSON-object line of a lane's `<executor>.events.log` with `charness_received_at`, the UTC time the carrier received it from the executor's pipe. Codex items and Muse envelopes carry no wall time of their own, so a lane that hit its time limit could not say how long a command or phase took. Non-JSON lines and the rest of each event's bytes are unchanged.
- `charness task status <task-id> --commands` reads that stamped log back and reports the lane's longest commands, starts per command family (test, lint, typecheck, merge), and time per phase. Without a task id the option is refused. A lane run before this release has an unstamped events log, so the report counts its command starts but gives no durations or phase times.

## Update

Run `charness update`, then use `charness version` to read back the installed version. No migration is required; the option is additive and existing `task status` calls behave as before.

